{
  "title": "25: Al-Furqaan الفرقان",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ الْفُرْقَانَ عَلٰى عَبْدِهٖ لِيَكُوْنَ لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ نَذِيْرَا ۙ‏(1)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE NAZZALAL AL-FURQAANA A’LAA A’ABDEH LEYAKOONA LIL-A’AALAMEENA NAZEERAA.\nBlessed is He who sent down ‘Furqan’ (the Distinction) upon His Servant (Muhammad) that he may be unto the worlds a Warner,\nاۨلَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَقَدَّرَهٗ تَقْدِيْرًا‏(2)\nLAZEE LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LAM YATTAKHEZ LAAHO LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL AL-MULKE WA KHALAQAL KULLA SHAY-IN FAQADDARAHU TAQDEERAA.\nHe, Who’s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and hath not taken He (unto Himself) any son, and there is not for Him any partner in the kingdom, and created He everything, and then planned He (for everything) a fixed measure.\nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً لَّا يَخْلُقُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَ وَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لِاَنْفُسِهِمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا وَّلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مَوْتًا وَّلَا حَيٰوةً وَّلَا نُشُوْرًا‏(3)\nWAT-TAKHAZOO MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL LAA YAKHLUQOONA SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA WA LAA YAMLEKOONA LE-ANFOSEHIM BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM WA LAA YAMLEKOONA MAWTAN WA LAA HAYWTAN WA LAA NUSHOORAN.\nYet have they adopted gods besides Him, which create not anything and they are them selves created, and own not for themselves any hurt or profit, and they control not death, nor life, nor raising the dead.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِفْكٌ اۨفْتَرٰٮهُ وَاَعَانَهٗ عَلَيْهِ قَوْمٌ اٰخَرُوْنَ‌‌ ۛۚ فَقَدْ جَآءُوْ ظُلْمًا وَّزُوْرًا ۛۚ‏(4)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA AEFKUN AFTARAAHU WAAA’AANAH A’LAYHE QAWMUN AAAKHAROONA FAQAD JAAA-OO ZULMAWN WWAZOORAN.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “This (Qur’an) is nothing but a lie which he (Our Apostle) hath forged and have helped him at it other people;” So indeed have they produced iniquity and uttered a slander.\nوَقَالُوْۤا اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ اكْتَتَبَهَا فَهِىَ تُمْلٰى عَلَيْهِ بُكْرَةً وَّاَصِيْلًا‏(5)\nWA QAALOO ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN AKTATABAHAA FAHEYA TUMLAA A’LAYHE BUKRATANW WA ASEELAA.\nAnd say they: “(they are the) tales of the ancient he hath got them written, so these are recited on him morn and even.\nقُلْ اَنْزَلَهُ الَّذِىْ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(6)\nQUL AANZALAHU LAZEE YA’LAMO AS-SERRA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ INNAHU KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nSay thou: “Hath sent it down He who knoweth the secrets of the heavens and the earth; Verily He is Oft-Forgiving, All- Merciful.\nوَقَالُوْا مَالِ هٰذَا الرَّسُوْلِ يَاْكُلُ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشِىْ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مَلَكٌ فَيَكُوْنَ مَعَهٗ نَذِيْرًا ۙ‏(7)\nWA QAALOO MAALE HAAZAA RASOOLE YAAKULU TA-A’AMA WAYAMSHEAA FIL AL-AASWAAQE LAWLAA UNZELA ELAYHE MALAKUN FA YAKOONA MA-A’HU NAZEERAN.\nAnd say they: “What sort of an apostle is this? He eateth food and he walketh about in the marts! Why hath not been sent unto him an angel that he be a warner with him?\nاَوْ يُلْقٰٓى اِلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ جَنَّةٌ يَّاْكُلُ مِنْهَا‌ ؕ وَقَالَ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(8)\nAW YULQAAA ELAYHE KANZUN AW TAKOONO LAHU JANNATUM YYAAKULU MINHAA WA QAALA ZAALEMOON IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA RAJULAN MMASHOORAN.\nOr be thrown down unto him a treasure, or there be for him a garden that he may eat of it?” and say the iniquitous: “Ye follow but a man bewitched\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلاً‏(9)\nAUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOOA LAKA AL-AAMSAALA FAZALLOOA FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAAN.\nSee thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) how they coin comparisons for thee! But they have gone astray, so they shall not be able to find the (right) way,\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ جَعَلَ لَكَ خَيْرًا مِّنْ ذٰ لِكَ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ۙ وَيَجْعَلْ لَّكَ قُصُوْرًا‏(10)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE IN SHAAA-AL JA-A’LA LAKA KHAYRAN MIN ZAA LEKA JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WA YAJ-A’L LAKA QUSOORAN.\nBlessed is He who, if He pleaseth, will give thee what is better than this {what all they say), gardens ’neath which flow rivers, and give thee mansions.\nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالسَّاعَةِ‌ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِمَنْ كَذَّبَ بِالسَّاعَةِ سَعِيْرًا‌ ۚ‏(11)\nBAL KAZZABOO BEALSSAAA’ATE WA A-ATADNAA LEMAN-Y KAZZABA BEALSSAAA’ATE SA-E’ERAA.\nNay! they belie the Hour (of Resurrection) and We have, ready for him who belieth the Hour, the burning fire.\nاِذَا رَاَتْهُمْ مِّنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ سَمِعُوْا لَهَا تَغَيُّظًا وَّزَفِيْرًا‏(12)\nEZAA RAATHUM MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED SAMEO’O LAHAA TAGHAYZAN WWAZAFEERAN.\nWhen it beholdeth them from afar, they shall hear its raging and roaring.\nوَاِذَاۤ اُلْقُوْا مِنْهَا مَكَانًا ضَيِّقًا مُّقَرَّنِيْنَ دَعَوْا هُنَالِكَ ثُبُوْرًا ؕ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ULQOO MINHAA MAKAANAN ZAYQAN MMUQARRANEENA DA-A’W HONAALEKAB SOBOORANW.\nAnd when they shall be flung into a narrow place therein, bound, they shall there call out for death;\nلَا تَدْعُوا الْيَوْمَ ثُبُوْرًا وَّاحِدًا وَّادْعُوْا ثُبُوْرًا كَثِيْرًا‏(14)\nLAA TADU’OOA YAWMA SOBOORANW WAAHEDANW WWAADU’OOA SOBOORANW KASEERAA.\n(It shall be said unto them) “Call ye not for this day for one death but call ye for death multiple!\nقُلْ اَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ اَمْ جَنَّةُ الْخُلْدِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ ‌ؕ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَزَآءً وَّمَصِيْرًا‏(15)\nQUL AAZAA LEKA KHAYRUL AM JANNATU AL-KHULDE LATEE WUE’EDA MUTTAQOON KAANAT LAHUM JA-ZAAA-AWN WWAMASEERAN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad): “Is this better or the eternal garden which hath been promised to the pious ones? that shall be for them a recompense and (their) destination.\nلَّهُمْ فِيْهَا مَا يَشَآءُوْنَ خٰلِدِيْنَ‌ ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ وَعْدًا مَّسْئُوْلًا‏(16)\nLAHUM FEEHAA MAA YASHAAOONA KHAALEDEENA KAANA A’LAA RABBEKA WA’DAN MMASOOLAN.\nFor them shall be therein whatever they desire abiding (in it)-, It is a promise from thy Lord worth to be prayed for.\nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقُوْلُ ءَاَنْتُمْ اَضْلَلْتُمْ عِبَادِىْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اَمْ هُمْ ضَلُّوا السَّبِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM WA MAA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAYAQOOLO A-ANTUM AAZLALTUM E’BAADEE HAAOOLAAA-E AM HUM ZALLOOA SABEELA.\nAnd on the day when He shall gather them, and what they serve besides God, He shall say: “Was it ye who beguiled these My servants, or themselves strayed they from the right path?\nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ مَا كَانَ يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ دُوْنِكَ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ وَ لٰكِنْ مَّتَّعْتَهُمْ وَاٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى نَسُوا الذِّكْرَ‌ۚ وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًۢا بُوْرًا‏(18)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA MAA KAANA LAHAA LANAA AN NNATTAKHEZA MIN DOONEKA MIN AAWLEEAAAA WA LAAKEN MMATTAA’TAHUM WA AA-BAAA-AHUM HATTAA NASUL KHASEYAR WA KAANOO QAWMAN BOORAA.\nThey will say, “Glory be to Thee! It behoved not for us that we take any friends besides Thee, but Thou didst provide them and their fathers to enjoy until they forsook Thy remembrance, while they were people to suffer perdition.\nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْكُمْ بِمَا تَقُوْلُوْنَۙ فَمَا تَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ صَرْفًا وَّلَا نَصْرًا‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّظْلِمْ مِّنْكُمْ نُذِقْهُ عَذَابًا كَبِيْرًا‏(19)\nFAQAD KAZZABOOKUM BEMAA TAQOOLOONA FAMAA TASTATEEU’OONA SARFAN WA LAA NASRAN WA MAN YYAZLEM MINKUM NUZEQHU A’ZAABAN KABEERAA.\n(Then will be said unto the idolaters) “so (now) indeed shall they belie you of what ye say, so ye shall not be able to avert (the doom) or to succour (yourselves) and whosoever be unjust of you, We shall cause taste great torment.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِنَّهُمْ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشُوْنَ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا بَعْضَكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ فِتْنَةً  ؕ اَتَصْبِرُوْنَ‌ۚ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ بَصِيْرًا‏(20)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA QABLAKA MENAL MURSALEEN ILLAA INNAHUM LAYAAKULOONA TA-A’AMA WAYAMSHOONA FIL AL-AASWAAQE WA JA-A’LNAA BAA’ZAKUM LE-BA’ZIN FETNATAN AATASBEROONA KAANAL RABBOKA BASEERAA.\nAnd We sent not any apostles before thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) but they certainly ate food and walked in the markets; and We have made some of you a trial for the others; will ye bear patiently? Your Lord is Ever-Seeing.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ اَوْ نَرٰى رَبَّنَا ؕ لَقَدِ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَعَتَوْ عُتُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(21)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA TAHMELOHUL AW NARAA RABBANAA LAQADE ASTAKBAROOA FEE ANFOSEHIM WAA’ATAW U’UTOOA KABEERAA.\nAnd say those who hope not of Our meeting: “Why have not angels been sent down upon us, or see we not Our Lord?” Indeed think they too high of themselves and have exceeded a great excess.\nيَوْمَ يَرَوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ لَا بُشْرٰى يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُجْرِمِيْنَ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ حِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(22)\nYAWMA YARAWNAL AL-MALAAAEKATA LAA BUSHRAA YAWMA-EZIN LILMUJREMEEN WA YAQOOLOONA HEJRAN MMAHJOORAN.\nOn the day when see they the angels, no glad tidings shall there be that day for the guilty, and they (the angels) shall say: “Forbidden it (the enjoyment) is, totally forbidden!\nوَقَدِمْنَاۤ اِلٰى مَا عَمِلُوْا مِنْ عَمَلٍ فَجَعَلْنٰهُ هَبَآءً مَّنْثُوْرًا‏(23)\nWAQADEMNAA ELAA MAA A’MELOO MIN A’AMALIN FA-JA-A’LNAAHO HABAAA-AM MANSOORAA.\nAnd (then) will We proceed unto what they have wrought of deeds, and We shall render them like unto the dust scattered in air.\nاَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ يَوْمَئِذٍ خَيْرٌ مُّسْتَقَرًّا وَّاَحْسَنُ مَقِيْلًا‏(24)\nASHAABUN JANNAH YAWMA-EZIN KHAYRUL MMUSTAQARRAN WWAAHSANU MAQEELAN.\nThe dwellers of the Garden {Paradise} that day shall be in a better abode and a better resting place.\nوَيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ السَّمَآءُ بِالْغَمَامِ وَنُزِّلَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(25)\nWA YAWMA TASHAQQAQU SAMAAA-O BE-GHAMAAME WANUZZELA TAHMELOHUL TANZEELAA.\nAnd on the day when the heavens shall burst asunder with cloud and the angels be sent down, descending (in ranks)\nاَلْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْحَقُّ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ‌ؕ وَكَانَ يَوْمًا عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَسِيْرًا‏(26)\nAALMULKU YAWMAEZE HAQQO LELRRAHMAANE KAANAL YAWMAN A’LAL KAAFEREEN A’ASEERAN.\nThe kingdom that day in truth shall belong to the Beneficent Lord; and the day for the infidels shall be very hard.\nوَيَوْمَ يَعَضُّ الظَّالِمُ عَلٰى يَدَيْهِ يَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِى اتَّخَذْتُ مَعَ الرَّسُوْلِ سَبِيْلًا‏(27)\nWA YAWMA YAA’AZZU AZ-ZAALEMU A’LAA YADAYHE YAQOOLO YAALAYTANEAA ATTAKHAZTU LAAHA RASOOLE SABEELAA.\nAnd on the day when the unjust one shall bite his hands saying: “Oh! would that I had taken with the Apostle the (same right) path!\nيٰوَيْلَتٰى لَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اَتَّخِذْ فُلَانًا خَلِيْلًا‏(28)\nYAAWAYLATAA LAYTANEAA LAM AATTAKHEZ FULAANAN KHALEELAN.\nOh! woe is me! would that I had not taken such a one as my friend!\nلَقَدْ اَضَلَّنِىْ عَنِ الذِّكْرِ بَعْدَ اِذْ جَآءَنِىْ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِلْاِنْسَانِ خَذُوْلًا‏(29)\nLAQAD AAZALLANEAA A’NIL AZ-ZEKRE BA’DA IZ JAAANEAA KAANAL SHAYTAANO INSAANIK KHAZOOLAN.\nHe did lead me astray from the Reminder after it had come unto me; and the Satan unto man was ever a detester!\nوَقَالَ الرَّسُوْلُ يٰرَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِى اتَّخَذُوْا هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ مَهْجُوْرًا‏(30)\nWA QAALA RASOOLO YAA RABBE INNAL QAWMEAA ATTAKHAZOOA HAAZAA QURAANA MAHJOORAN.\nAnd shall say (out) the Apostle (that day) “O’ my Lord! Verily my people have held this Qur’an as a vain forsaken thing!\nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّا مِّنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‌ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ هَادِيًا وَّنَصِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA LEKULLIM NABEAAAIN A’DUWWAL MENAL AL-MUJREMEENA KAFAA BERABBEKA HAADEEA WWANASEERAN.\nAnd thus We did appoint for every apostle an enemy from among the guilty ones; But sufficient is thy Lord as a Guide and a Helper (for thee).\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ جُمْلَةً وَّاحِدَةً‌  ‌ۛۚ كَذٰلِكَ ‌ۛۚ لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ‌ وَرَتَّلْنٰهُ تَرْتِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA NUZZELA A’LAYHE QUR-AANO JUMLATAN WAAHEDATAN KAZAALEKA LENUSABBETA BEHI FUAADAKA WARATTALNAAHU QUR-AANA.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “Why hast not the Qur’an been sent down upon him all at one (time)?” Thus (is it revealed) that We may strengthen by it thy heart, and We have recited it (unto thee) in well-arranged gradual stages.\nوَلَا يَاْتُوْنَكَ بِمَثَلٍ اِلَّا جِئْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَحْسَنَ تَفْسِيْرًا ؕ‏(33)\nWA LAA YAATOONAKA BEMASALIN ILLAA JENAAKA BIL-HAQQE WA AHSANAL TAFSEERAN.\nAnd they (the infidels) shall bring not unto thee any argument, but We shall bring unto thee the truth and the best explanation (of it).\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُحْشَرُوْنَ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(34)\nLAZEENA YUHSHAROONA A’LAA SEEMAAHUM ELAA JAHANNAMA OOLAAA-EKA HOWA MMAKAANAN WWAAZALLU SABEELAA.\nThose who shall be gathered upon their faces unto Hell, those shall have the worst place, and straying farther away from the (right) path.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلْنَا مَعَهٗۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ وَزِيْرًا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(35)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LNAA MA-A’HU AAKHAAHU AALO WAZEERAN.\nAnd indeed We gave Moses the Book and We did appoint with him his brother Aaron (as his) assistant.\nفَقُلْنَا اذْهَبَاۤ اِلَى الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاؕ فَدَمَّرْنٰهُمْ تَدْمِيْرًاؕ‏(36)\nFAQULNAA AZHABAA ELAL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BEAAAYAATENAA FA DAMMARNAAHUM TADMEERAN.\nAnd said We: “Go ye both unto the people who belie Our signs!” so We did destroy them with utter destruction.\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ لَّمَّا كَذَّبُوا الرُّسُلَ اَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ وَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ لِلنَّاسِ اٰيَةً ‌ ؕ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا ‌ۖ‌ ۚ‏(37)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN LAMMAA KAZZABOOA AR-RUSULA AAGHRAQNAAHUM WA JA-A’LNAAHUM LIN-NAASE AAYATAL WA A-ATADNAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd the people of Noah, when they belied the apostles, We drowned them, and made them a sign for mankind; and We have prepared for the unjust, a painful chastisement.\nوَّعَادًا وَّثَمُوْدَا۟ وَ اَصْحٰبَ الرَّسِّ وَقُرُوْنًۢا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ كَثِيْرًا‏(38)\nWWAA’AADAN WA SAMOODAA WA MASALAN AR-RASSE WA QOROONAN BAYNA ZAA LEKA KASEERAA.\nAnd the (tribes of) ’Ad and Thamud and the inhabitants of Ar-Rass, and generations between them, in a great number.\nوَكُلًّا ضَرَبْنَا لَهُ الْاَمْثَالَ‌ وَكُلًّا تَبَّرْنَا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(39)\nWAKULLAN ZARABNAA LAHUL AL-AAMSAALA WAKULLAN TABBARNAA TATBEERAN.\nAnd unto each of them We did give examples and every one (of them) We did destroy with utter extermination.\nوَلَقَدْ اَتَوْا عَلَى الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْۤ اُمْطِرَتْ مَطَرَ السَّوْءِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا يَرَوْنَهَا ‌ۚ بَلْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ نُشُوْرًا‏(40)\nWA LAQAD ATAW A’LAL QARYAH LATEE AUMTERAT MATARA SAW A-FALAM YAKOONOOA YARAWNAHAA BAL KAANOO LAA YARJOON NUSHOORAN.\nAnd indeed they have passed by the town on which was rained a fatal rain; did they not then see it? Nay! they hope not to be raised again (after their death).\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْكَ اِنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْنَكَ اِلَّا هُزُوًا ؕ اَهٰذَا الَّذِىْ بَعَثَ اللّٰهُ رَسُوْلًا‏(41)\nWA EZAA RAAWKA IN YYATTAKHEZOONAKA ILLAA HOZOWANW AAHAAZAA LAZEE BA-A’SA LAAHO RASOOLAM.\nAnd when they see thee, they take thee not for aught but in ridicule; (saying) “What! Is this he whom God hath raised to be an apostle?\nاِنْ كَادَ لَيُضِلُّنَا عَنْ اٰلِهَتِنَا لَوْ لَاۤ اَنْ صَبَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ حِيْنَ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذَابَ مَنْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nIN KAADA LAYUZELLUNAA A’N AAALEHATENAA LAW LAA AN SABARNAA A’LAYHAA WA SAWFA YA’LAMOON HEENA YARAWNAL A’ZAABA MAN AZALLO SABEELAA.\nHe hath well-nigh led us astray from our gods had we not been adhered to them steadfastly!” And they will know when they see the chastisement, who is straying farther away from the (right) path.\nاَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(43)\nA-RA-AYTA MANIS TAKHAZA AELAAHAH HAWHU AAFAANTA TAKOONO A’LAYHE WAKEELAA.\nHast thou seen him who taketh his vain inclinations for his god? Wouldst thou then be a guardian over him?\nاَمْ تَحْسَبُ اَنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ يَسْمَعُوْنَ اَوْ يَعْقِلُوْنَ‌ ؕ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا كَالْاَنْعَامِ‌ بَلْ هُمْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(44)\nAM TAHSABU ANNAL AKSARAHUM YAS-MA-O’ONA AW YA’QELOON IN HUM ILLAA KAALAANA’AAME BAL HUM AZALLO SABEELAA.\nThinkest thou that most of them do hear or understand? they are not but like the cattle; Nay! they are farther astray from the (right) path.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ كَيْفَ مَدَّ الظِّلَّ‌ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ لَجَعَلَهٗ سَاكِنًا‌ ۚ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا الشَّمْسَ عَلَيْهِ دَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(45)\nALAM TARA ELAA RABBEKA KAYFA MADDA AZ-ZELLA WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAJAA’ALAH SAAKENAN SUMMA JA-A’LNAA SHAMSA A’LAYHE DALEELAN.\nSeest thou not unto (the might of) thy Lord, how He extendeth the shadow? And had He willed He would certainly have made it stationary, then We have made the sun to be its guide,\nثُمَّ قَبَضْنٰهُ اِلَيْنَا قَبْضًا يَّسِيْرًا‏(46)\nSUMMA QABAZNAAHU ELAYNAA QABZAN YASEERANW.\nThen We draw it in unto Us, by an easy (gradual) contraction.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا وَّالنَّوْمَ سُبَاتًا وَّجَعَلَ النَّهَارَ نُشُوْرًا‏(47)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LEBAASANW WWAALNNAWMA SOBAATANW ANHAARAWN NAHAARA NUSHOORAN.\nAnd He it is who hath made for you the night as a covering, and the sleep a rest, and made the day to rise up again.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ۚ وَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً طَهُوْرًا ۙ‏(48)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ARSALA REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY FEE WA ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN TAHOORAA.\nAnd He it is Who sendeth the winds as the herald of the glad tidings going before His mercy (rain), and We send down from heaven water pure,\nلِّنُحْیِۦَ بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا وَّنُسْقِيَهٗ مِمَّا خَلَقْنَاۤ اَنْعَامًا وَّاَنَاسِىَّ كَثِيْرًا‏(49)\nLENUH BEHI BALDATAN MMAYTAN WWANUSQEEH MIMMAA KHALAQNAL AN-A’AMAN WWAANAASEAAAA KASEERAA.\nThat We may give life by it to a dead land, and We give it for drink, out of what We have created, to cattle and men in numbers multiple.\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنٰهُ بَيْنَهُمْ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ‌ ۖ ا فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(50)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAAHU BAYNAHUM LEEZZAKKAROOA A FAABAAA AAKSARU NAASE ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nAnd indeed We distribute it (water) to them that they may be (thankfully) mindful, but content not the great number of the people but to be thankless.\nوَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَبَعَثْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ قَرْيَةٍ نَّذِيْرًا ‌ۖ ‏(51)\nWA LAW SHE’NAA LABAA’ASNAA FEE KULLE QARYATINW NNAZEERAN.\nAnd had We willed, certainly had We raised up a warner in every town.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ وَ جَاهِدْهُمْ بِهٖ جِهَادًا كَبِيْرًا‏(52)\nFALAA LAA KAAFEREEN WA JAAHEDHUM BEHI JEHAADAN KABEERAA.\nSo yield thou not to infidels, and strive against them with it a strenuous strife.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ مَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ هٰذَا عَذْبٌ فُرَاتٌ وَّهٰذَا مِلْحٌ‌ اُجَاجٌ ۚ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًا وَّحِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(53)\nWA HOWA LAZEE MARAJAL WA HAAZAA A’AZBUN FURAATUN WWAHAAZAA MELHUN AUJAAJUN WA BAYNAHOMAA BARZAKHAN WWAHEJRAN MMAHJOORAN.\nAnd He it is Who hath made the two seas join and flow together, one palatable and sweet, and the other salt and bitter; and yet hath made He between the two a barrier, and a barrage impassable.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ مِنَ الْمَآءِ بَشَرًا فَجَعَلَهٗ نَسَبًا وَّ صِهْرًا‌ ؕ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ قَدِيْرًا‏(54)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL MENAL AL-MAAE BASHARAN FA-JA-A’LAHU NASABAN WA SEHRAN KAANAL RABBOKA QADEERAA.\nAnd He it is Who hath created man of water, and made him related in blood and in wedlock; and thy Lord is All- Powerful.\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَلَا يَضُرُّهُمْ‌ؕ وَكَانَ الْكَافِرُ عَلٰى رَبِّهٖ ظَهِيْرًا‏(55)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UHUM WA LAA YAZURRUHUM KAANAL AL-KAAFERU A’LAA RABBEHI ZAHEERAL.\nAnd yet worship they besides God, (things) which neither profit them nor harm them; And the infidel had (ever) been an aider (of evil) against thy Lord.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا‏(56)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MUBASSHERAN WA NAZEERANW.\nAnd We sent thee not (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) but a Bearer of glad tidings and a Warner.\nقُلْ مَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ سَبِيْلًا‏(57)\nQUL MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN ILLAA MAN SHAAA-AL AN YYATTAKHEZA ELAA RABBEHI SABEELAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I ask ye not aught of any recompense (for my ministry) save that he, who will, take the way unto his Lord!\nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِهٖ‌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِهٖ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرَ ا‌ ۛۚ ۙ‏(58)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL HAYYE LAZEE LAA YAMOOTO WASABBEH BEHAMDEH KAFAA BEHI BEZUNOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERA A.\nAnd rely thou on the (Ever) Living One who dieth not, and celebrate thou with His praise; and sufficient is He as being All-Aware of the faults of His servants.\nاۨلَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ ‌ۛۚ اَلرَّحْمٰنُ فَسْئَلْ بِهٖ خَبِيْرًا‏(59)\nLAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL AR-RAHMAAN FASAL BEHI KHABEERAA.\n(He) Who created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six days, and is firmly established on the Throne (of Supreme Authority); the Beneficent (God); Ask thou about Him (only) from (the one who is) aware.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اسْجُدُوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ قَالُوْا وَمَا الرَّحْمٰنُ اَنَسْجُدُ لِمَا تَاْمُرُنَا وَزَادَهُمْ نُفُوْرًا ۩‏(60)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUL JODOO LELRRAHMAANE QAALOO WA MAA RAHMAANO AANASJUDU LEMAKH TAAMURUNAA WA ZAADAHUM NUFOORAN.\nAnd when it is said unto them: “Prostrate ye in obeisance unto ‘Rahman’ (the Beneficent, i.e., God),” say they: “Who is ‘Rahman’ (the Beneficent, i.e., God)? Shall we prostrate in obeisance unto what thou biddest us?” and it (only) addeth to their flight (from the Truth)\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ فِى السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا وَّجَعَلَ فِيْهَا سِرٰجًا وَّقَمَرًا مُّنِيْرًا‏(61)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE JA-A’LA FIL SAMAAA-E BUROOJAN ANHAARAWN FEEHAA SERAAJAN WWAQAMARAN MONEERAA.\nBlessed is He who made in the heavens the constellations and made in it a lamp (the sun) and the moon illuminating.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ خِلْفَةً لِّمَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يَّذَّكَّرَ اَوْ اَرَادَ شُكُوْرًا‏(62)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA KHELFATAN LEMAN ARAADA AN YYAZZAKKARA AW ARAADA SHOKOORAA.\nAnd He it is who hath made the night and the day to succeed each other for him who desireth to reflect or desireth to be thankful.\nوَعِبَادُ الرَّحْمٰنِ الَّذِيْنَ يَمْشُوْنَ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ هَوْنًا وَّاِذَا خَاطَبَهُمُ الْجٰهِلُوْنَ قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‏(63)\nWAE’EBAADU RAHMAANIR LAZEENA YAMSHOONA A’LAL ARZE HAWNAN WWAAZAA KHAATABAHUMU AL-JAAHELOONA QAALOO SALAAMAA.\nAnd the servants of the Beneficent (God) are they who walk on the earth humbly; and when address them the ignorants, say they: Salam (Peace).\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَبِيْتُوْنَ لِرَبِّهِمْ سُجَّدًا وَّقِيَامًا‏(64)\nWAL LAZEENA YABEETOONA LE-RABBEHIM SUJJADANW WWAQEEAMAN.\nAnd those who pass the night in prostrating (in obeisance) unto their Lord and standing.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا اصْرِفْ عَنَّا عَذَابَ جَهَنَّمَ ‌ۖ  اِنَّ عَذَابَهَا كَانَ غَرَامًا ‌ۖ ‏(65)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA ASREF WAGH A’ZAABAL JAHANNAMA INNAL A’AZAABAHAA KAANA GHARAAMAN.\nAnd those who say (pray): “O’ Our Lord! Turn Thou away from us the torment of the Hell, verily the torment of it is a lasting affliction.\nاِنَّهَا سَآءَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(66)\nINNAHAA SAAAT MUSTAQARRAN WWAMUQAAMAN.\nVerily, it is an evil abode and (an evil) station.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا لَمْ يُسْرِفُوْا وَلَمْ يَقْتُرُوْا وَكَانَ بَيْنَ ذٰلِكَ قَوَامًا‏(67)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ANFAQOO LAM YUSREFOOA WA LAM YAQTUROOA KAANAL BAYNA ZAALEKA QAWAAMAN.\nAnd those who when they spend, are neither extravagant and nor niggardly but are stationed between the two (extremes).\nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَدْعُوْنَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ وَلَا يَقْتُلُوْنَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا يَزْنُوْنَ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ يَلْقَ اَثَامًا ۙ‏(68)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YAD-O’ONA LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR WA LAA YAQTULOONA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA LAA YAZNOONA WA MAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA YALQA AASAAMAN.\nAnd those who call not with God any other gods, and slay not a soul which God hath forbidden (to do it) save with a right (to do so), and who commit not adultery; and whosoever doeth this shall find a requital of the sin,\nيُضٰعَفْ لَهُ الْعَذَابُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَيَخْلُدْ فِيْهٖ مُهَانًا ۖ ‏(69)\nYUZAAA’AF LAHUL A’ZAABO YAWMA QEYAAMATE WAYAKHLUD FEEH MUHAANAN.\nFor him shall be doubled, the torment on the Day of Resurrection, and for ever shall they abide in it, in ignominy\nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ عَمَلًاصَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ حَسَنٰتٍ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(70)\nILLAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA A’AMALANSAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YUBADDELU LAAHO SAYYEAATEHIM HASANAATIN KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nSave he who turneth repentant and believeth and doeth good deeds; then these are they who, God changeth (their) evil deeds to good ones; And God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nوَمَنْ تَابَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاِنَّهٗ يَتُوْبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَتَابًا‏(71)\nWA MAN TAABA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-INNAHU YATOOBU ELAL LAAHE MATAABAN.\nAnd whosoever repenteth and doeth good and verily turneth he unto God a (sincere) turning,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَشْهَدُوْنَ الزُّوْرَۙ وَ اِذَا مَرُّوْا بِاللَّغْوِ مَرُّوْا كِرَامًا‏(72)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YASHHADOONA AZ-ZOORA WA EZAA MARROO BIL-LAGHWE MARROO KERAAMAN.\nAnd those who bear not witness to what is false, and when pass they by what is vain, pass they in dignity.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَمْ يَخِرُّوْا عَلَيْهَا صُمًّا وَّعُمْيَانًا‏(73)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ZUKKEROOA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM LAM YAKHERROOA A’LAYHAA SUMMAN WWAU’UMYAANAN.\nAnd those who, when admonish ed by the signs of their Lord, fall not down thereat deaf and blind.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا هَبْ لَنَا مِنْ اَزْوَاجِنَا وَذُرِّيّٰتِنَا قُرَّةَ اَعْيُنٍ وَّاجْعَلْنَا لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِمَامًا‏(74)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA HAB LANAA MIN AAZWAAJENAA WAZURREETENAA QURRATA AAA’YUNIN WWAAJA’ALNAA LILMUTTAQEEN AEMAAMAN.\nAnd those who say “O’ Our Lord! Grant us from our wives and our offspring the joy of our eyes, and make us for the pious ones (their) Imams\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُجْزَوْنَ الْغُرْفَةَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا وَيُلَقَّوْنَ فِيْهَا تَحِيَّةً وَّسَلٰمًا ۙ‏(75)\nOOLAAA-EKA YUJZAWNA AL-GHURFATA BEMAA SABAROO WAYULAQQAWNA FEEHAA TAHEETAN WWASALAAMAN.\nThese shall be rewarded with the high stations (in Paradise) for their patience, and they shall meet therein with honours and salutation,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ حَسُنَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(76)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA HASUNAT MUSTAQARRAN WWAMUQAAMAN.\nAbiding therein; Excellent the abode, and the resting place.\nقُلْ مَا يَعْبَؤُا بِكُمْ رَبِّىْ لَوْلَا دُعَآؤُكُمْ‌ۚ فَقَدْ كَذَّبْتُمْ فَسَوْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِزَامًا‏(77)\nQUL MAA YAA’BAUA BEKUM RABBEE LAWLAA DUA’AAUKUM FAQAD KAZZABTUM FA-SAWFA LAHUL LEZAAMAN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto the disbelievers: “My Lord would (also) care not for you had it not been your prayer (unto Him), but ye indeed have belied (the Truth), and soon ye shall be (in) the grip (of the inevitable)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Furqan (The Criterion)\nThis Surah has 77 verses and it is ‘Makki’. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a person who recites this Surah will be taken to Jannah without questioning, provided he believes in the Day of Judgement and the Raising of the Dead (from the graves).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that Allah (s.w.t.) will never send His punishment upon any person who recites this Surah every night. The reciter of this Surah will also gain a highly status in the hereafter. The person who writes this Surah and keeps it in his possession will never be harmed by the vermin of this earth."
